## 9. Example Policy Logic

A non-limiting policy expression may be:

```text
IF
    user.eligibility_class includes "approved_researcher"
AND organization.verified_type includes "accredited_research_institution"
AND affiliation.status = "current"
AND resource.permitted_purpose includes request.purpose
AND authentication.assurance >= required_assurance
THEN
    issue role "restricted_compute_researcher"
    with:
        project_scope = request.project
        export = prohibited
        network_access = allowlisted
        session_duration = 8 hours
        monitoring = enhanced
ELSE IF
    organization.verification_status = "provisional"
THEN
    require human approval
    and provide metadata-only access
ELSE
    deny
```

Policies may use scoring, decision tables, graphs, machine-readable rules, learned models, or combinations thereof. A learned model may recommend a decision while a deterministic policy layer enforces mandatory boundaries.

