## 10. Illustrative Use Cases

### 10.1 Shared Research Computing

Researchers from universities, nonprofit laboratories, government institutions, and commercial organizations share computing resources. Dataset access and export controls vary according to verified organization type, researcher status, project approval, and data-use agreement.

### 10.2 Regulated Data Environment

A secure environment hosts healthcare, financial, educational, or governmental data. Access is granted only to users with appropriate qualifications and verified affiliations with approved organization types.

### 10.3 Multi-Tenant AI or High-Performance Computing Platform

The system allocates models, accelerators, software, and network access according to user eligibility, organization category, approved use, and risk tier. Certain users receive isolated execution without access to model weights or underlying datasets.

### 10.4 Supplier and Partner Access

Employees of verified suppliers or partners receive narrowly scoped, temporary roles. A change in contractual status or organization verification automatically terminates access.

### 10.5 Public-Interest or Sponsored Access

An otherwise ineligible external user may receive access through sponsorship by an eligible organization. The sponsor’s authority, the user’s classification, and the project scope jointly determine permissions.

